kind: graph
semantic_diff: >-
  No digest of a living document or of a run input anywhere in the graph.
  13 hunks, 27 added lines against 27 removed, every one prose inside
  existing structure: node ids, outcome sets, roles, effects, consumes and
  produces lists, required_evidence lists, check styles, evaluators, failure
  routes, edges and control endpoints are equal between the two graphs,
  proved by parsing both and comparing the skeletons field by field
  (32 nodes / 95 edges / 5 control endpoints unchanged).

  (1) BLOCK-SCOPED PLAN LAPS HAND BACK THE TOUCHED BLOCKS ONLY. Five sites
  (increment_plan_draft subject, review_campaign_design, draft_increment_plan
  body and plan_drafted outcome, assemble_design_record) said the lap returns
  "touched blocks with their new digests, must-hold digests of every other
  block" and the lead "byte-checks every untouched block". The plan is a
  living document that must shrink (references/artifact-layout.md section
  4.12: "nothing binds a block of the increment plan"), so every legitimate
  deletion lap moved every block digest, and the lead's read of the diff was
  already the instrument. Now: the touched blocks, nothing else; the lead
  reads the diff to confirm no unnamed block moved.

  (2) RUN STATE POINTS AT THE PLAN'S REVISION-LOG LINE, NOT A PER-EDIT
  DIGEST. Four sites (increment_lap_record subject, review_campaign_design
  bookkeeping edits and re-entry brief, scope_next_increment lap record)
  recorded "the plan digest" after each edit or collapse. A digest of a
  document that changes on every bookkeeping edit is a change detector the
  revision log already is; the campaign re-derived block pins at 23 plan
  revisions and every one reproduced.

  (3) THE PIN SCREEN COMPARES THE CAMPAIGN'S TARGET PIN TO ITS SOURCE. Two
  sites in screen_pin_and_progress said "pin digest compared byte-identical
  against pinned_release"; no digest of pinned_release ever existed, and the
  value the screen actually holds is the campaign's campaign_target_pins
  entry, whose declared source is pinned_release for a backport route and
  the kickoff-declared upgrade base for an upgrade route (state contract).
  The text now names that compare.

  (4) THE MEASURER CONFIRMS INPUTS AGAINST THE REGISTRATION RECORD. Three
  sites in capture_baseline_reference (purpose, activity, baseline_unusable)
  said "hash-pinned inputs" and "a pinned input whose live digest
  contradicts its design-record pin"; the plugin ships no script that
  computes or compares such a digest, and the design record declares no such
  field. The registration record does declare the comparator set's
  "identity, config, versions" (preregister_acceptance), so the inputs are
  now the ones the registration record names, each confirmed against the
  identity it declares, and baseline_unusable names an input whose live
  identity contradicts the registration record.

  WHY, GENERALLY: pave-spec 9.14.3 (pave-init 2.5.4) - content-address only
  what never changes again; a pin on a file still being edited makes every
  fix a new file plus a re-pin of all that named it, and the writer of the
  bytes also wrote the number. The kept digests are the ones a tool computes
  on a write-once subject: the ledger chain in revisions.yaml, the
  kickoff-criteria digest in narrow_delta_scoped (:286) and the registration
  re-entry digest (:1288) - both write-once subjects - the registration
  record's timestamp check (comparators_preregistered, :320-325), and
  measurement captures. Nothing here names a tool, a model or a metric, and
  it removes text rather than adding it.

  FIELD EVIDENCE: GLM 5.3 Flash campaign audit of 2026-09-09 (eight-agent
  workflow, 34 claims confirmed / 9 weakened / 0 refuted): 4 real catches by
  any hash check, none a wrong measurement or wrong shipped code; 13 fires on
  benign differences that each cost a re-cut lap; 27 blocks that re-pinned
  and proceeded unchanged; at least 7 typed-digest defects introduced by the
  protocol; 1,437 of 8,662 increments files (16.6%) in pinning-only name
  families. Release-layer copies of the same sentences (agents, SKILL.md,
  references, Codex agents) are corrected in 1.5.4; this revision is the
  graph copy. Reviewed by an independent adversarial reviewer (fable) as part
  of the 1.5.4 batch; its HIGH finding on the pin-screen wording is applied in
  (3) before landing.
envelope_check: changed_with_approval
plan_evidence: verified
usage_evidence: field
changelog_entry: >-
  Revision 7 (graph): no digest of a living document or run input. Block-scoped
  plan laps hand back the touched blocks only and the lead reads the diff (five
  sites; the "must-hold digests of every other block" clause contradicted the
  plugin's own layout rule that nothing binds a block of the living plan). Run
  state points at the plan's revision-log line instead of a per-edit plan digest
  (four sites). The pin screen compares the campaign's target-pin entry to its
  declared source (two sites). The measurer captures against the inputs the
  registration record names, each confirmed against the identity it declares,
  and baseline_unusable names a live identity that contradicts that record
  (three sites). Counts unchanged at 32 nodes, 95 edges, 5 control endpoints;
  27 added lines against 27 removed in 13 hunks. Rule: pave-spec 9.14.3
  (pave-init 2.5.4). Field evidence: the GLM 5.3 campaign audit of 2026-09-09 -
  23 plan re-pin occasions all reproducing, 4 real catches none a wrong
  measurement, at least 7 typed-digest defects.
